1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,660
One of China's biggest military
problems wasn't weapons.

2
00:00:04,300 --> 00:00:07,340
It was finding horses
strong enough to use them.

3
00:00:08,340 --> 00:00:12,820
In the second century BCE, the most
dangerous enemy of the Han dynasty

4
00:00:12,820 --> 00:00:18,600
lived on horseback: the Xiongnu,
nomads of the northern steppe.

5
00:00:19,400 --> 00:00:21,720
Emperor Wu had been
fighting them for decades,

6
00:00:21,720 --> 00:00:25,380
and to catch riders, he needed
better horses than his own.

7
00:00:25,740 --> 00:00:27,860
Then word came from the far west.

8
00:00:28,840 --> 00:00:32,980
More than two thousand miles
away, in the Ferghana Valley,

9
00:00:33,220 --> 00:00:36,240
lay a kingdom the Chinese called Dayuan.

10
00:00:37,140 --> 00:00:42,360
Its horses, people said, sweated blood,
and were descended from horses of heaven.

11
00:00:43,460 --> 00:00:46,620
The emperor sent an envoy
with a thousand pieces of

12
00:00:46,620 --> 00:00:50,220
gold and a horse made of
gold, to buy the best of them.

13
00:00:51,300 --> 00:00:53,480
Dayuan's nobles refused.
